    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Bryson Stott** (71.06) headline the LawDog lineup as our primary offensive anchors. **Taylor Ward** benefits significantly from the matchup against Lodolo; the combination of a favorable park factor and a substantial boost from the platoon advantage against a southpaw makes him the high-water mark for our daily efficiency score. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** remains a high-floor play despite the proximity to a tough pitcher in Avila. While the team\u2019s aggregate speed profile is vital for our pursuit of SB, **Lawrence Butler** (70.17) is a must-start today, fueled by a +10% park boost and a strong platoon split that positions him to capitalize on his #4 hole in the lineup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's bench was **Drew Gilbert** (49.05). He was the final cut for the outfield, narrowly edged out by **Daulton Varsho** and **Jung Hoo Lee**. While **Drew Gilbert** benefits from the favorable conditions in his park and possesses an elite sprint speed that typically warrants inclusion, his lower spot in the batting order (-6% penalty) ultimately dragged his efficiency score below the threshold required to displace our starters. We are also closely monitoring the utility slot, where **Luis Arraez** (62.57) remains locked in; his leadoff role (+10% order bonus) and positive park adjustments provide the stability we need to balance the volatility of our power-heavy outfielders.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the current health landscape. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** continuing their stints on the IL, our depth is being tested, and we must be diligent in preserving our game caps. While the matchups for **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Masyn Winn** are technically \"Strong\" based on their scores, both face mid-tier starters like Sproat and Assad who carry enough efficiency to warrant caution. No weather-related threats are currently projected to impact play, but owners should keep a close eye on the late-afternoon lineups to ensure no last-minute rest days for our core assets like **Jonathan Aranda** or **Cal Raleigh**.",
